    owner: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.serving.srv1_serving_launch", decl_name: "srv1_serving_launch"),
    inputs: "the declared GPU group and its resolved device identities; the cap readbacks the group requires",
    superseded: "--device nvidia.com/gpu=all and route device_index 0, which silently change meaning when a card is added",
    waits_on: ["GPU power-cap realization"],
    closes_on: "the engine starts only after its own devices qualify (Requires= and After= on a cap step that fails on refusal); a one-card configuration stays evaluable while a second card is pending; TP=2 requires both members and never degrades to TP=1",
    standing: MigrationStartedHere { what: "gunbc.serving.srv1_serving_launch now declares srv1_serving_gpu_group (the one powered card, gpu_board_04) and CONSTRUCTS the installed wrapper's `--device` from it: srv1_serving_docker_device_words_of renders one `--device nvidia.com/gpu=<UUID>` per member (the UUID resolved through gunbc.fleet.gpu_device_observation current_gpu_device_observations_of, admitted through gunbc.fleet.gpu_power_state_policy admit_gpu_cap_against), and builds the wrapper body (the script the boot unit installs for the next boot) only inside srv1_serving_wrapper's Installable arm, where the group resolved to a non-empty admitted set; a group that does not resolve is Srv1ServingWrapperRefused and has NO body, so neither `nvidia.com/gpu=all` nor a GPU-less `docker run` is writable, and the deploy's install leg matches that same value. The route's served device ordinal is derived from the declared group (srv1_serving_served_device_rank), no longer the literal 0. The host copy the RUNNING container was launched from (still `all`) is retained as history in srv1_serving_wrapper_running_body and pinned by gunbc.host.srv1_serving_startup_receipt; srv1_serving_wrapper_adoption types the installed-vs-running gap PendingOperatorRelaunch — a DECLARED relaunch obligation the OPERATOR performs, never an auto-restart. The power-limit readback that lets a device run stays owned by gunbc.fleet.gpu_power_cap_converge, enforced on the real path by the engine unit's Requires= on the cap unit. Readiness belongs to the selected configuration: the one-card group resolves while gpu_board_01 (Workstation) is pending, and a TP=2 group refuses rather than degrading to TP=1 (asserted in test.claim.serving.srv1_serving_launch_witness and test.claim.live_deploy.live_deploy_apply_plan_witness)." },
