    inputs: "the exact device group, placement, interconnect, software, caps and workload a reading was taken on",
    superseded: "readings from a rented two-card PCIe 5 host read as if they described srv1's PCIe 4 pair",
    waits_on: ["a cross-topology read on this host -- the same instrument at TP=2 and at 2xTP=1 -- named in srv1_collective_read_obligation. The unloaded re-run this row used to wait on is EXECUTED and recorded (srv1_collective_read_executed_2026_11_09, 2026-11-09T22:40:35Z): the 2x delta between the arms did not survive an unloaded host, so it is no longer a reason to distrust these readings; what stays open is that the TP margin itself is still unexplained."],
    closes_on: "evidence from another configuration cannot qualify this one; srv1's own P2P, NCCL and serving readings exist before TP=2 is admitted",
    standing: MigrationStartedHere { what: "the Workstation card half of the wait is closed: it enumerates (gunbc.fleet.gpu_device_observation, 2026-11-08). srv1's own interconnect readings exist and are first-hand: peer access refused in both directions, the chipset named as the cause by the two `nvidia-smi topo -p2p r` CNS tokens that were read (the CUDA runtime also refuses, unattributed -- it has no cause to give), the pair at NODE across two host bridges, both links negotiating Gen4 x16 below the Gen5 x16 the cards advertise, ACS redirecting at both root ports, the SMMU translating both GPU groups (gunbc.fleet.gpu_interconnect_observation). The NCCL half landed too, on 2026-11-08 22:22 UTC at the operator's request: an eight-row first-hand all-reduce sweep in a short-lived container with both CDI GPUs (default arm and NCCL_P2P_DISABLE=1, four sizes each), which also retired the relayed claim that the two arms behave the same -- the two arms separated from 256 KiB up while naming the same SHM/direct transport, and that separation was typed as a hypothesis rather than read as a mechanism. (The numbers and the comparison live in gunbc.fleet.gpu_interconnect_observation and its witness; this row does not carry figures.) What keeps this row open is one obligation, not a missing reading: the throughput comparison itself landed on main with #16104 (gunbc.serving.srv1_topology_comparison, 2026-11-09), so all three of P2P, NCCL and serving readings named by closes_on are in-tree; the sweep re-take landed on 2026-11-09T22:40:35Z with BOTH replicas stopped (srv1_collective_read_executed_2026_11_09), and the 2x gap did NOT survive an unloaded host: it was the serving replicas holding memory, so it no longer qualifies the serving comparison. What keeps this row open now is the cross-topology read -- the same instrument at TP=2 and at 2xTP=1 on this host -- plus the reversed-arm-order and transport-named controls, all three named in srv1_collective_read_obligation" },
